C. Practical interpretation
  The best missed targets are not the most famous targets.  They are
  problems where the repo already has a carrier but has not built the
  correct finite toy model: decks for reconstruction, color-critical
  unit-distance graphs, Kakeya/Falconer finite-field incidence ledgers,
  sunflower cores inside OCF hypergraphs, and union-closed frequency
  carriers.  Clay-scale problems remain useful as negative controls,
  not as first attack surfaces.
